# MCP env template for the 1Password MCP server.
# Resolved at spawn-time via: op run --env-file <this-file> -- <command>
# Only list secrets this server needs.
#
# Note: OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN is the bootstrap root-of-trust —
# it is injected by the cloud-env config (not fetched via op://).
# We pass it through from the parent process env using the special
# `op run` syntax of leaving the value blank to inherit from env.
# However, `op run --env-file` with `VAR=op://...` form will fail for
# the SA token itself (chicken-and-egg). Instead we rely on Claude Code
# inheriting OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN from the container env block
# (set via Anthropic's cloud-env config, NOT settings.json).
#
# The 1Password MCP server needs OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN to
# authenticate to 1Password. It is NOT a secret fetched via op://;
# it IS already present in the process env from the cloud-env config.
# The server inherits it via normal env inheritance — no op:// ref needed.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of op:// refs because the 1Password
# MCP's auth token is the SA token itself (not fetchable via op://).
# The server will inherit OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN from the process env.
